{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:07aac43ed9671dba","name":"Dangers of Study","source":{"id":"source:reference-07aac43ed9671dba","title":"Dangers of Study","revision":24391,"timestamp":"2024-10-30T19:36:08Z","sha256":"6440097e1f8ca010a31cb8dcbc23b5281341a14a8f89997e70d82115c774b22c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24391","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Dangers%20of%20Study&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-07aac43ed9671dba","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The galaxy is vast, and even after thousands of years of study, only a tiny fraction of the planets, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beasts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beasts"}," that it contains have been discovered, much less studied. Jedi Padawans are warned of the untold dangers that await them in the galactic vastness, which is not to say that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," should destroy every dangerous beast they encounter. However, if one is to fulfill the role of galactic peacekeeper, one must be aware of the dangers that the galaxy abides.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The creatures and individuals described here are but a sample of the strange, exotic, and lethal dangers that a Jedi might encounter during an adventure. Some creatures are relegated to a single planet or even a single location, but others have managed to spread across the galaxy. In rare circumstances, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," have deemed some of these creatures, notably those altered by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},", as grave threats that must be eliminated to help bring harmony to the galaxy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," are interested in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beasts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beasts"}," that have sensitivity to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," and the ability to wield it in some manner. The Jedi Council has numerous ongoing programs in place to discover, catalog, and study Force-sensitive creatures, both to learn more about them and to gain a greater insight into their own assumptions on how ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," manifests itself. One thing is for certain- most creatures are dangerous in their own right, but those that can command ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," tend to be smarter, faster, tougher, or deadlier than normal.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Darksiders"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following section provides a rogues' gallery of Force-sensitive villains who might cross paths with the heroes during their exploits. These villains range from low-level lackeys to unique, named characters with sinister motives and evil agendas. Because of their strong ties to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", these NPCs make great enemies for groups of heroes containing one or more ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," characters.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Gamemaster who has no intention of using the villains described herein is still encouraged to use the villains' statistics. With a simple name substitution, any of the darksiders presented here can fit into a GM's home campaign.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AFFILIATIONS\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Azrakel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Azrakel","referenceId":"reference:443d204a9802265e"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Prophets of the Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Prophets_of_the_Dark_Side","referenceId":"reference:2e7d5ec2ca3829a6"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blackguard Minion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blackguard_Minion","referenceId":"reference:08f15d2229d4a0c0"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Blackguard Wilder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blackguard_Wilder","referenceId":"reference:e7381df7683493e4"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Blackguard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Blackguard","referenceId":"reference:e4d5dd88946cc424"},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","